DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260609T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260609T140000
SUMMARY:CPAN Series: Normal Grief and Loss vs. PTSD
LOCATION:Virtual
DESCRIPTION:In this installment of the CPAN Webinar Series\, Raja Kiani \, 
 M.D.\, presents “Normal Grief and Loss vs. PTSD.” Register to attend. Prim
 ary care physicians (PCPs) currently demonstrate a significant gap in know
 ledge and clinical competence regarding the identification and management 
 of mental health disorders in youth. This professional practice gap is pri
 marily attributed to insufficient training and limited access to mental he
 alth resources. As a result\, PCPs often serve as the first point of conta
 ct for families dealing with adolescent mental and behavioral health issue
 s\, yet they report lacking the necessary skills to effectively screen\, a
 ssess\, and treat conditions such as depression\, anxiety\, suicidal ideat
 ion\, and behavioral disorders. This series aims to enhance PCPs’ capabili
 ties in recognizing and managing mental health conditions to improve outco
 mes for youth within their clinical practice. For more information about t
 he event\, email cpd@bcm.edu .\\n\\nRegister: https://events.teams.microso
 ft.com/event/e226cefe-d74b-45ad-b253-659e2e10fde7@a83dba53-124d-4d32-88f0-
 b72889a9e926\\n\\nEvent page: https://dellmed.utexas.edu/events/cpan-serie
 s-normal-grief-loss-ptsd
URL:https://dellmed.utexas.edu/events/cpan-series-normal-grief-loss-ptsd
END:VEVENT
